{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531537-a-kinetic-conundrum","id":1531537,"title":"A Kinetic Conundrum","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-26T13:18:48-08:00","id":1531537,"title":"A Kinetic Conundrum","content":"A friend and I had a discussion recently around the ability of a mage with Forces 2 where they can intensify or reduce the kinetics of an impact.<br /> <br /> In M20: How Do You Do That? pg. 30 it says \u2018If the blow would normally inflict bashing damage, and the Forces Effects adds to that damage, then the damage also becomes lethal instead of bashing because it hits so much harder. If, for example, Khan bends physics to intensify a kick, and his player rolls four successes for that kick, then the opponent must try and soak five successes\u2019 worth of lethal damage... if she can!\u2019<br /> <br /> This is not what\u2019s up for debate. No, what my friend originally asked me was this, \u2018Do you think that by using this ability a mage could make a vampire take lethal damage from a gun?\u2019 (Admittedly I don\u2019t remember the exact phrasing of the question but the essence of it is the same.) On pg. 281 of the V20 rulebook it says this \u2018Against mortals, firearms are considered lethal damage. Versus vampires, firearms are considered bashing damage unless the head is targeted (see \u201cTargeting,\u201d p. 274), in which case the damage is considered lethal.\u2019<br /> <br /> So I said \u2018No, I don\u2019t think that particular use of the forces sphere would make one of the kindred take lethal from a gun.\u2019 My reasoning being that firearms deal lethal damage already, the lethal damage that vampires take from said guns are usually considered bashing. He justified himself by saying \u2018It would actually, because the mage would be turning the bashing damage they normally would be getting from the gun into lethal.\u2019<br /> <br /> So\u2026 you see the issue at hand. Am I crazy here? The reason I don\u2019t think this would work is because this use of Forces is exerting control over things OUTSIDE of the party that\u2019s being harmed by it. Transforming a punch into a lethal strike due to the sheer kinetic output of that strike being increased. A vampire taking bashing damage from guns in something inherent to their being, like soaking lethal damage. So how would this ability turn the bashing damage the lethal was converted into back into lethal? I feel that in order to do something like this you\u2019d need an effect that changes some fundamental aspect of the vampire, a Life+Matter effect maybe? (By the way I know you could also use Forces or Prime to make it agg, but that's not the point of the question.)<br /> <br /> Would love to get some outside opinions!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28390-doctornode","name":"DoctorNode","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T19:34:33-08:00","id":1531577,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m with you. The bashing damage from bullets is a special property of vampires not a property of bullets. The way bullets do lethal damage simply doesn\u2019t matter to the undead as much, and Forces doesn\u2019t change how the bullet does damage. <br /> <br /> The only way to enhance the kinetic power of a bullet enough to do lethal damage to them is ramp it up enough to fill up the health track so that it overflows.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T12:18:28-08:00","id":1531792,"title":"","content":"I believe you can turn bullets lethal into aggravated and thus harm vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T17:11:16-08:00","id":1531821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531537-a-kinetic-conundrum?p=1531792#post1531792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe you can turn bullets lethal into aggravated and thus harm vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, in several different ways. A Forces rote might make the bullets burn, fire dies aggravated to Vampires. Some Prime rotes should work to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","na